{%- comment -%}
  Casify brand fonts, self-hosted. Render in <head> before theme.css.

  The files are assets/cv-f-*.woff2, taken unchanged from Google Fonts (Playfair Display,
  Libre Baskerville, Parisienne and Caveat are OFL; Special Elite is Apache 2.0). The rules
  below are Google's css2 rules for the same families, weights and display=swap, latin and
  latin-ext subsets only. A browser downloads a file only when the page has text in that
  file's unicode-range, so unused faces cost nothing.

  They used to come from fonts.googleapis.com: a render-blocking stylesheet on another
  server, so a first visit opened two extra connections (fonts.googleapis.com, then
  fonts.gstatic.com) before the page could paint. Inline rules need no request, and the
  font files arrive over the connection the page already has open to the store's CDN.
  Caveat was pulled in by an @import at the top of cv-pdp-home.css and cv-pdp-slip.css,
  which chained the same two connections behind those stylesheets on product pages.
{%- endcomment -%}
